Here’s the GraphQL query you’d send (you’ll still need to put your API key in the `Authorization` header):

```graphql
{
  communityComments(domain: "test4.org", cursor: "cur456", limit: 10) {
    edges {
      node {
        id
        context
      }
    }
    pageInfo {
      hasNextPage
      endCursor
    }
  }
}
```

Make sure to set the request header:

```
Authorization: Bearer key123
```

This will return only the `id` and `context` fields for each comment.
